      "title": "Q: Dumb vs coverage-guided?",
      "seconds": 90,
      "answerMarkdown": "**A:** **Dumb** fuzzing **doesn't** **learn** from **execution**-cheap but **shallow**. **Coverage-guided** uses **instrumentation** to **prefer** **mutations** that **hit** **new** **edges**-**much** **deeper** **bug** **discovery** **per** **CPU** **hour**."
    },
    {
      "id": "p91550c2ad14a7a",
      "cluster": "Mechanics",
      "title": "Q: What makes a bad fuzz harness?",
      "seconds": 90,
      "answerMarkdown": "**A:** **Too** **large** **surface** per **iteration**, **shared** **mutable** **state** **without** **reset**, **network** **I/O** **inside** **the** **loop**, or **timeouts** **too** **short** **so** **legit** **paths** **never** **complete**.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "id": "pa62dc87dfeef3f",
      "cluster": "Operations",
      "title": "Q: Where should fuzzing run?",
      "seconds": 90,
      "answerMarkdown": "**A:** **Dedicated** **workers** or **nightly** **CI**-not **every** **PR** **if** **runtime** **is** **hours**; **gate** **releases** on **no** **new** **high** **severity** **crashes** **in** **main** **branch** **campaigns**."
    },
    {
      "id": "p69e517878a7537",
      "cluster": "Operations",
      "title": "Q: OSS-Fuzz\u2014what is it?",
      "seconds": 90,
      "answerMarkdown": "**A:** **Google**-operated **service** **pattern** for **open** **source**: **maintainers** **submit** **projects** with **harnesses**; **continuous** **fuzzing** **finds** **bugs** **early**.\n\n---"
